Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile a comprehensive report of the exploration results:

## Exploration Report: Ability System & Camera System Patterns

Based on my thorough exploration of the WjWorld project, here's a complete analysis of the existing patterns for creating a camera toggle ability:

---

### **1. ABILITY BASE CLASS PATTERN**
**File:** `/Source/WjWorld/AbilitySystem/Abilities/WjWorldGameplayAbilityBase.h/cpp`

**Key Features:**
- **Base Class:** Inherits from `UGameplayAbility`
- **Instancing Policy:** `InstancedPerActor` (most abilities use this)
- **Net Execution Policy:** `LocalPredicted` (for client-side prediction)
- **Blocked Tags:** All abilities block `State_Eliminated` tag (prevents abilities when dead)
- **Cooldown System:** 
  - `CooldownDuration` property for duration
  - `CooldownTags` for tag-based cooldown tracking
  - Custom `GetCooldownTags()` that merges parent + custom tags
  - Uses `UGE_AbilityCooldown` GameplayEffect
- **GameState Integration:**
  - Checks `AllowedAbilityTags` from `AWjWorldGameStatePlay` (per-minigame ability restrictions)
  - Only activates during `EGamePhase::Playing` phase
- **UI Metadata:**
  - `AbilityName` (FText) for UI display
  - `AbilityIcon` (UTexture2D) for UI display
- **Virtual Charge System Interface:**
  ```cpp
  virtual bool IsChargeBased() const { return false; }
  virtual int32 GetCurrentCharges() const { return 0; }
  virtual int32 GetMaxCharges() const { return 0; }
  virtual float GetChargeRefillTimeRemaining() const { return 0.f; }
  virtual FText GetPromptDescription() const { return FText::GetEmpty(); }
  ```

---

### **2. SIMPLE ABILITY EXAMPLE: GA_Jump**
**Files:** `/Source/WjWorld/AbilitySystem/Abilities/GA_Jump.h/cpp`

**Pattern - Immediate Execution Ability:**
```cpp
// Constructor setup
UGA_Jump::UGA_Jump()
{
    InstancingPolicy = EGameplayAbilityInstancingPolicy::InstancedPerActor;
    NetExecutionPolicy = EGameplayAbilityNetExecutionPolicy::LocalPredicted;

    FGameplayTagContainer AssetTags;
    AssetTags.AddTag(WjWorldGameplayTag::Ability_Jump());
    SetAssetTags(AssetTags);

    // Blocked by other states
    ActivationBlockedTags.AddTag(WjWorldGameplayTag::State_SpawnBrickPreview());
    ActivationBlockedTags.AddTag(WjWorldGameplayTag::State_LiftBrickCarry());

    // Cooldown setup
    CooldownTags.AddTag(WjWorldGameplayTag::Cooldown_Jump());

    AbilityName = NSLOCTEXT("Abilities", "Jump", "점프");
}

// CanActivateAbility override for custom validation
bool UGA_Jump::CanActivateAbility(...) const
{
    if (!Super::CanActivateAbility(...)) return false;

    const ACharacter* Character = CastChecked<ACharacter>(ActorInfo->AvatarActor.Get());
    return Character && Character->CanJump();
}

// Main ability execution
void UGA_Jump::ActivateAbility(...)
{
    Super::ActivateAbility(...);

    if (HasAuthorityOrPredictionKey(ActorInfo, &ActivationInfo))
    {
        if (!CommitAbility(Handle, ActorInfo, ActivationInfo))
        {
            EndAbility(Handle, ActorInfo, ActivationInfo, true, true);
            return;
        }

        ACharacter* Character = CastChecked<ACharacter>(ActorInfo->AvatarActor.Get());
        Character->Jump();
    }
}

// Input release handling
void UGA_Jump::InputReleased(...)
{
    ACharacter* Character = CastChecked<ACharacter>(ActorInfo->AvatarActor.Get());
    Character->StopJumping();
    EndAbility(Handle, ActorInfo, ActivationInfo, true, false);
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Simple, stateless ability - no preview or complex state management
- Uses `CanActivateAbility()` for validation beyond base checks
- Handles both input press and release
- Uses `CommitAbility()` before executing effect
- Calls `EndAbility()` when complete

---

### **3. CAMERA SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE**

#### **A. Camera Mode Enum**
**File:** `/Source/WjWorld/GamePlay/Camera/WjCameraTypes.h`
```cpp
UENUM()
enum class ECharacterCameraMode : uint8
{
    TopDown,
    ThirdPerson,
    FirstPerson
};
```

#### **B. Camera Component**
**File:** `/Source/WjWorld/GamePlay/Camera/WjWorldGameplayCameraComponent.h/cpp`

```cpp
DECLARE_DYNAMIC_MULTICAST_DELEGATE_OneParam(FCameraModeSetSignature, const FGameplayTag&, CameraMode);

UCLASS()
class WJWORLD_API UWjWorldGameplayCameraComponent : public USceneComponent
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    const FGameplayTag& GetCurrentCameraMode() const;
    void SetCameraMode(const FGameplayTag& InCameraModeTag);

private:
    FGameplayTag CurrentCameraMode;

    UPROPERTY(BlueprintAssignable)
    FCameraModeSetSignature OnCameraModeSetted;  // Broadcasts when mode changes
};
```

**Implementation:**
```cpp
void UWjWorldGameplayCameraComponent::SetCameraMode(const FGameplayTag& InCameraModeTag)
{
    CurrentCameraMode = InCameraModeTag;
    OnCameraModeSetted.Broadcast(InCameraModeTag);  // Broadcast to listeners
}
```

#### **C. Character Camera Setup**
**File:** `/Source/WjWorld/Core/Base/WjWorldCharacterBase.h`

```cpp
// In constructor:
GamePlayCamera = CreateDefaultSubobject<UGameplayCameraComponent>(TEXT("GamePlayCamera"));
GamePlayCamera->SetupAttachment(RootComponent);
GamePlayCamera->SetAutoActivate(false);  // Manually activated

// In SetupPlayerInputComponent:
GamePlayCamera->Activate();  // Activated after InputComponent setup

// Camera mode properties:
UPROPERTY(EditDefaultsOnly, Category = "Camera")
ECharacterCameraMode StartCameraMode = ECharacterCameraMode::TopDown;

UPROPERTY(VisibleAnywhere, BlueprintReadOnly)
FGameplayTag CameraMode;

// Public method to change camera:
void SetCharacterViewMode(ECharacterCameraMode NewViewMode);
void SetCharacterViewMode(const FGameplayTag& NewViewMode);
```

**Camera Mode Setter Implementation:**
```cpp
void AWjWorldCharacterBase::SetCharacterViewMode(ECharacterCameraMode NewViewMode)
{
    FGameplayTag NewCameraMode = FGameplayTag::EmptyTag;

    switch (NewViewMode)
    {
    case ECharacterCameraMode::TopDown:
        NewCameraMode = WjWorldGameplayTag::Camera_TopDown();
        break;
    case ECharacterCameraMode::ThirdPerson:
        NewCameraMode = WjWorldGameplayTag::Camera_ThirdPerson();
        break;
    case ECharacterCameraMode::FirstPerson:
        NewCameraMode = WjWorldGameplayTag::Camera_FirstPerson();
        break;
    }

    SetCharacterViewMode(NewCameraMode);
}

void AWjWorldCharacterBase::SetCharacterViewMode(const FGameplayTag& NewViewMode)
{
    CameraMode = NewViewMode;
    OnCharacterViewModeChanged.Broadcast(NewViewMode);  // Broadcast to listeners
}
